            "horizons.fy0.capex",
            "horizons.fy1.capex",
            "horizons.fy2.capex",
            "quarterly_path.fq1_27.capex"
          ]
        },
        {
          "claim": "Q3 refinancing of ~$476M first-lien debt reduces total debt by $97M and annual interest expense by an estimated $62M; cash interest expected ~65% below pre-emergence ~$400M, toward a ~$145M post-refi run-rate.",
          "source": "0000895419-26-000024:ex991q3-26.htm:b0000016 and 10-Q MD&A b0000563",
          "horizon": "Q4 FY26 and FY27",
          "flows_into": [
            "income_statement.interest_expense",
            "horizons.fy1.net_income",
            "quarterly_path.fq1_27.net_income"
          ]
        },
        {
          "claim": "AI datacenter revenue grew ~30% QoQ in Q3; 10kV MOSFET and next-gen TOLT portfolio purpose-built for AI/infrastructure; auto engagement on 800V+ architectures.",
          "source": "Q3 FY26 earnings presentation p.7; 0000895419-26-000024:ex991q3-26.htm:b0000006",
          "horizon": "FY27-FY29",
          "flows_into": [
            "quarterly_path.fq1_27.revenue",
            "quarterly_path.fq4_27.revenue",
            "horizons.fy1.revenue",
            "horizons.fy2.revenue",
            "horizons.fy3.revenue"
          ]
        },
        {
          "claim": "Durham now materials-only after 150mm device fab shutdown; continuing to qualify customers on 200mm and exploring 300mm materials. Factory start-up costs have ended; underutilization remains until demand fills Siler City/Durham materials capacity.",
          "source": "Q3 presentation p.6; 10-Q MD&A b0000498 / b0000509",
          "horizon": "FY26-FY28",
          "flows_into": [
            "income_statement.factory_startup",
            "income_statement.gross_profit",
            "horizons.fy1.gross_profit",
            "horizons.fy2.gross_profit"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "buy_triggers": [
        {
          "marker": "Quarterly revenue at or above $170M with GAAP gross profit at or above zero (first non-negative GM quarter).",
          "checkable_at": "FY27 Form 10-Q (any of FQ1-FQ4 FY27)"
        },
        {
          "marker": "Two consecutive quarters of CFO better than -$40M and capex at or below $35M, demonstrating the self-funded plan actually funds itself.",
          "checkable_at": "FY27 Q2 or Q3 Form 10-Q cash-flow statement"
        },
        {
          "marker": "Power-products revenue sequential growth of at least 10% with materials revenue no longer declining, confirming 200mm quals and AI/industrial design-wins are converting.",
          "checkable_at": "FY27 Q1 or Q2 earnings 8-K product-line revenue table"
        }
      ],
      "sell_triggers": [
        {
          "marker": "Quarterly revenue still at or below $150M at the FY27 Q2 print, implying the post-Durham-EOL hangover and EV softness have not troughed.",
          "checkable_at": "FY27 Q2 earnings 8-K / 10-Q"
        },
        {
          "marker": "Cash and cash equivalents plus short-term investments falling through $700M combined with a single-quarter CFO worse than -$80M, signaling liquidity is being consumed faster than the post-refi runway assumed.",
          "checkable_at": "Any FY27 10-Q balance sheet and cash-flow statement"
        },
        {
          "marker": "Restructuring and other expenses above $25M in a quarter, or a new factory-start-up line item reappearing, indicating another capacity or footprint reset.",
          "checkable_at": "Any subsequent earnings 8-K income statement"
        }
      ],
      "what_must_be_true": "Mohawk Valley 200mm utilization and Siler City/Durham materials quals must convert the already-built footprint into less-negative, then positive, gross profit before operating cash burn plus maintenance capex exhausts the ~$1.2B Q3 liquidity. Auto does not have to boom; AI/industrial/A&D plus a materials trough are enough if opex stays near the post-restructuring run-rate and cash interest actually prints near the $145M post-refi level. If utilization stays depressed, underutilization in COGS keeps GM negative into FY28 and the equity account erodes via accumulated deficit even with no new large CapEx."
    },
    "preview_note": "WOLF reports Q4 FY26 against a $140–160M revenue guide issued with the Q3 print. We expect $146M, a touch below the midpoint: Durham 150mm EOL pull-ins are gone, materials customers are still destocking, auto remains soft, and the 30% QoQ AI-datacenter growth is off a small base. GAAP GM should stay negative (we have −24% vs −27% in Q3) as Siler City/Durham underutilization persists; opex is guided flat and we model a modest drop in restructuring now that Durham device is shut. The P&L swing is interest: the March 19 1L paydown is advertised as −$62M annualized, but Q4 still includes a stub of pre-refi coupon plus the June 1L cash-rate step-up, so we take interest to $38M, not the full $36M run-rate. Non-op will look much worse than Q3’s $46M income, which was derivative marks and a $10M contingent-cash gain that will not repeat. Cash burn remains the real scorecard — we have CFO −$95M and FCF −$127M, taking cash to ~$588M. The stock reaction will turn on (1) whether revenue clears $150M, (2) any evidence GM is inflecting rather than just “still negative,” and (3) the Q1 FY27 guide; we expect $145–165M, not a clean re-acceleration.",
    "reasoning": "Q4 is a trough-ish print inside a $140–160 guide, not a recovery quarter. Filed Q3 revenue was $150.2M at the prior midpoint; management explicitly blamed 1H pull-forward (Durham EOL buys, bankruptcy second-sourcing) and weak EV. Those effects do not reverse in one quarter, so I sit $4M below the guide midpoint at $146M. Cost of revenue $181M holds underutilization as a structural COGS item (Siler City now in production, Durham materials underloaded) and only a small sequential GM improvement. OpEx follows the “approximately flat” guide on R&D/SG&A, with restructuring fading from $10.6M to $6.0M. Interest steps down from $52.1M on the $476M 1L takeout but not all the way to the $145M annualized cash-interest slide, because the June coupon step-up and a mid-quarter close leave residual cost; $38M is the compromise. Non-operating income collapses versus Q3 because the $28.7M derivative gain and $10M contingent-cash gain are non-recurring. Bridge uses WOLF’s own non-GAAP add-backs (SBC, restructuring/facility, project/transformation, DIC amortization, disposal, residual derivative). Cash: D&A stays on the fresh-start ~$31M run-rate; WC is no longer a large source after Q2’s $90M working-capital harvest; capex stays maintenance-plus-qual at $32M, consistent with “no significant additional CapEx.” No financing event is assumed in Q4. FY26 revenue is the sum of the three printed quarters plus $146M ($661.5M). FY26 GAAP NI is positive only because of the $1.06B emergence-day reorganization gain; operations lose money all year. FY27–29 assume a slow utilization-led GM recovery (first positive GP in FQ4 FY27), opex discipline, and maintenance capex — not a return to the pre-bankruptcy growth/CapEx model. Cash still burns through FY29 on this path; that is the binding constraint and the reason buy/sell triggers are written on revenue, GM sign, and CFO, not on a multiple."
  },
